00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.959
Um, but when it comes to the ideal
gas law, this is always referring to

00:01:49.959 --> 00:01:54.410
what the current condition is of the
gas after the reaction occurred, or

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:56.050
even before the reaction occurred.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.520
So what is the condition?

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:02.280
Now the big thing about this is you
